# Crime Scene AI — Smart Evidence Capture Assistant

Live demo: field officer uploads a crime-scene photo → the vision layer
extracts objects / stains / text (each with confidence + source + basis) →
the reasoning layer drafts a report in **both English and Hindi** → the
officer **edits and confirms** the narrative → only the confirmed report is
logged to the case file with chain-of-custody metadata → pattern matching
against past confirmed cases.

## What runs out of the box

This Space is fully functional with **zero configuration** (offline demo mode):

| Component | Behavior in this Space |
|---|---|
| Object detection | HSV/geometry heuristics (`source: "heuristic"`) — real YOLOv8n is opt-in via `backend/requirements-ai.txt` |
| Blood-like stain | Red-hue HSV heuristic + morphology + area/saturation basis (never a verdict) |
| OCR | Optional — install `pytesseract` + a Tesseract binary (`apt install tesseract-ocr` on Linux) to enable |
| Reasoning | Offline mock LLM (`source: "mock"`) — set `OPENAI_API_KEY` as a Space secret to use a real LLM |
| Case log | SQLite, per-instance (ephemeral — fine for a demo) |

Everything degrades gracefully and always explains *why* in `processing_notes` —
no silent behavior.

## How to use

1. Open the app (it starts on the root URL of this Space).
2. Upload any scene photo (phone photos work best — EXIF GPS/time are read
   automatically; you can also type coordinates).
3. Review the draft: objects, stain candidates, OCR text, narrative
   (English + Hindi), anomaly flags and next steps.
4. Edit the narrative if needed, then **Confirm & log case** — the confirmed
   report enters the case file with an audit trail and pattern matches.

## Self-hosting / local run

```bash
python -m venv .venv && .\.venv\Scripts\activate   # (Linux: source .venv/bin/activate)
pip install -r requirements.txt
python gradio_app.py      # http://localhost:7860
```

## Enabling the real models (optional)

| Component | How | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| YOLOv8n objects | `pip install -r backend/requirements-ai.txt`; first run downloads `yolov8n.pt` (~6 MB) | `source: "yolo"` detections (knife/car/bag/…) |
| OCR (Tesseract) | `pip install pytesseract` + Tesseract binary (`apt install tesseract-ocr`) | `ocr` entries (reads Devanagari better with EasyOCR) |
| Real LLM reasoning | add `OPENAI_API_KEY` (and optionally `OPENAI_BASE_URL`, `OPENAI_MODEL`) as a Space secret | `llm.source: "openai"` narrative |

## Honest limitations (demo-grade, not evidence-grade)

- Detections are **suggestions for triage**, never admissible evidence. The
  officer-confirmation step is the evidence boundary.
- The "blood-like stain" heuristic detects red-dominant regions — it cannot
  distinguish blood from paint/rust/curry, and the report says so.
- ELA tamper flag is a heuristic, always reported with `"inconclusive"` framing.
- Pattern matching scores shared object categories — a triage aid, not
  case-linking evidence.
- Case data is stored in the Space's ephemeral filesystem and is reset on
  restart.

## API

The FastAPI backend still exposes its full API surface — used for the main
React demo (`GET /api/health`, `POST /api/upload`, `POST /api/cases`,
`GET /api/cases[/{id}]`, `GET /api/images/{image_id}`). This Gradio Space
drives the same pipeline (`backend/app/pipeline.py`) directly.

Built for the Smart India Hackathon (SIH) demo track. Backend FastAPI ·
frontend React (Vite) · this card is a Gradio Space.